faq:
  - q: How much water do I need for rice?
    a: The amount of water depends on the type of rice and cooking method. As a simple starting point, a ratio of around 2 parts water to 1 part rice can be used for some types of white rice.
  - q: How much water do I need for 100g of rice?
    a: With a 2:1 water-to-rice ratio, you would use approximately 200 ml of water for 100 g of rice.
  - q: How much water do I need for 200g of rice?
    a: With a 2:1 ratio, 200 g of rice would require approximately 400 ml of water.
  - q: Is the rice-to-water ratio the same for every type of rice?
    a: No. Different varieties such as basmati, jasmine, brown and short-grain rice can require different amounts of water. When available, follow the cooking instructions on the package.
  - q: Can I calculate water for any amount of rice?
    a: Yes. Enter the amount of rice and select the water-to-rice ratio that best matches the rice and cooking method you are using.

